<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Qatar</h1><p class="st-meta">1868 CE – 1971 CE · capital Doha</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Qatar under the Al Thani, from its recognition by Britain in 1868 through Ottoman and British protection to independence in 1971.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Qatar's coast had been dominated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain's</a> Al <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalifa">Khalifa</a>. After a destructive war between them, the British envoy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lewis-pelly">Lewis Pelly</a> signed an agreement with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-bin-thani">Muhammad bin Thani of Doha</a> in 1868, recognising him as the peninsula's leader. Ottoman troops arrived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doha">Doha</a> in 1871.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jassim-bin-muhammad-al-thani">Jassim bin Muhammad Al Thani</a>, ruler from 1878 to 1913, is regarded as founder of the state; he defeated an Ottoman force at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-al-wajbah">al-Wajbah</a> in 1893. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-qatar">Qatar</a> lived from pearling and fishing and was poor and sparsely populated. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> withdrew during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-qatari-treaty">Anglo-Qatari Treaty</a> of 1916 made Qatar a British protected state. The collapse of the pearl trade in the 1930s caused hardship.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Oil was found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dukhan">Dukhan</a> in 1939 and exported from 1949, funding development. When <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> withdrew from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Gulf</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-qatar">Qatar</a> declined to join the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a> and became the independent State of Qatar on 3 September 1971.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1868 CE – 1971 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:96.88%;width:2.05%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1868 CE – 1971 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Doha</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad bin Thani, Jassim bin Muhammad Al Thani, Ahmad bin Ali Al Thani</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam (Wahhabi)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/qatar">Qatar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Qatar, Emirate of Qatar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-qatar" aria-label="Sheikhdom of Qatar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6045 1248 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sheikhdom of Qatar lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6365 1504L6335 1476M6365 1504L5709 970M6365 1504L4997 651M6365 1504L6365 1504"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6335 1476h0M5709 970h0M4997 651h0M6365 1504h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6365 1504h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6365 1504h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Doha. <a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-qatar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
